        "postCreatedAt": "2026-10-28T06:32:56.072Z",
        "postUpdatedAt": "2026-10-28T06:32:56.072Z",
        "fetchedAt": "2026-10-29T07:25:27.611Z",
        "responseUrl": "https://community.n8n.io/t/325067.json",
        "responseSha256": "e40872426e8cf52f2c9d8695debf29405e96c8953dbbc2390b7ce8824a9e9480",
        "normalizedSha256": "45a152e72373c302db7bce57cd251f65c7e67ac19697cebdbcce37f694c07edc",
        "normalizedLength": 1023,
        "retainedCharacters": 928,
        "omittedCharacters": 95,
        "spans": [
          {
            "kind": "context",
            "start": 0,
            "end": 262,
            "text": "Sharing a simple pattern I use for tracking hiring at target companies. Workflow: Schedule Trigger (daily) → Apify node (“Run an Actor and get dataset”) → IF item count > 0 → Slack. In the Apify node, run the Actor birchwood-data/ats-job-scraper with input like:",
            "sha256": "57bf2db7b206d1f69c4f00c5662fd79323bf690d722ad96b84835d615ec027bc"
          },
          {
            "kind": "context",
            "start": 357,
            "end": 1023,
            "text": "For Workday career sites use birchwood-data/workday-jobs-scraper the same way. In the Slack node, post {{$json.title}} – {{$json.location}} – {{$json.url}} . Because the Actor remembers which jobs it has already seen between runs, each run returns only new postings, so no dedupe logic is needed in n8n. A quiet day costs almost nothing, since the Actors are pay-per-result (Workday is $0.002 per returned job). Actors: Greenhouse, Lever & Ashby Job Scraper | ATS Jobs API · Apify and Workday Jobs Scraper | myworkdayjobs.com API · Apify Disclosure: I built both Actors. Happy to share the workflow JSON if that’s useful, and feedback on what to add next is welcome.",
            "sha256": "757fa149df8e6c2f35cb2c7e1f576cc6bafca549842107bd255db201a6d4a469"
          }
        ],
        "packetSha256": "ee13dee9ea92e960d51496618640af7bccdd9407f76f903af7bbe86a2d713698"
      },
      "verifiedAt": "2026-10-29T07:25:27.611Z",
